Narrative & RationaleLoading Weights: The model parameters themselves can exceed GPU memory. Quantization and DeepSpeed Offloading address this directly by making the weights smaller or streaming them.Running Attention: Traditional attention requires large activation storage and has O(N^2) memory scaling. FlashAttention and LSH Attention reduce or manage this overhead.Storing KV Caches: Multi-turn dialogues and RAG with large context windows can balloon the KV cache. Multi-Query/Grouped-Query Attention and PagedAttention (vLLM) mitigate this.Fine-Tuning: Storing optimizer states for every parameter can be prohibitive. QLoRA drastically reduces these overheads by quantizing base weights and only training small LoRA adapters. Meanwhile, DeepSpeed can offload the leftover to CPU/NVMe if needed.Inference Serving: Once the model is fine-tuned, deploying it at scale for RAG or autonomous agents requires memory-optimized serving strategies like vLLM with PagedAttention or FlashAttention kernels to handle high throughput.
